    "body": "local commit 2fe41a2 on issue/208-axis-point-concurrency (stacked on PR #204 at 7fff05c, not pushed yet). Approach: a point-concurrency guard (`crates/motion/src/multiaxis/axis_point.rs`). It finds the point the inliers' normal lines meet best (area least trimmed squares). When the lines through that point carry at least half the inlier area, those facets must pass the coarseness gate about the axis on their own bearings. On an isotropic part, a pole axis is no longer tilted by the refinement. Pins, each failing on the base: plate + boss at (10,0) refused, single-band D-flat + cross-hole shaft refused, and the 60 mm cube + off-centre boss refused in 1 and 5 bands (from the #204 re-review). A single-band bar still fits Z. motion lib axis (47), multiaxis*/rotary*/turning* and the app drilling_cross*/lathe_*/turning* suites are green, and clippy on motion+app is clean.\n",
    "author_association": "OWNER",
    "pin": null,
